 "description": "\u00a728 step 4: where CloudSheetOverlay.Draw's ~80 us/call goes. Shares, not absolutes -- eight simultaneous arms put Circinus's per-call transpile cost in every row. The parent arm is kept so the children can be summed against it; an unexplained gap is a finding in itself. REQUIREDMODS IS LOAD-BEARING HERE, and its absence is why this file could not measure anything as first committed: every arm in it is a Circinus arm, and with Circinus not in the run's mod list circinus_available reads 0, every timing reads 0, and the wide recording tolerances on the _calls and _total_ms pins let all of them PASS. Only circinus_available and the _patched pins fail, which is exactly what they are there for -- a table of zeros must not be readable as a fast mod. CIRC_DECKILLUM IS ALSO GONE, for a different reason. CloudSheetMath.DeckIllumination has two overloads, so AccessTools.Method by name alone throws Ambiguous match and Circinus can never arm it -- which made circ_deckillum_patched a pin that could not pass and this file therefore a scenario that always reported FAIL however healthy the run. A gate that always fails is a gate nobody reads. The arm stays registered in ProbeRegistration so it can be pinned again the day CircinusProbe learns to take parameter types; until then the cost it would have measured is still inside circ_clouddraw.",
